desc: DVS timecode to jog (timecode vinyl / CD, Pioneer DJ PLX-CRSS12)
//tags: reascratch dvs timecode turntable
//author: ReaScratch
//
// (⚪209) Reads a DVS control tone (the stereo signal of a timecode vinyl or CD, or the Serato control tone that the
// Pioneer DJ PLX-CRSS12 sends from its PHONO OUT in Digital Vinyl mode) from the track's audio input and turns the
// record's movement into jog MIDI for a ReaScratch deck. The setup script puts it on a track "DVS A in" / "DVS B in"
// (record armed, input = the audio interface's pair, monitoring on) whose MIDI goes to the deck's engine track
// (a send: MIDI only). The deck's preset "DVS (timecode, PLX-CRSS12)" reads it: relative jog CC 34 on the deck's
// channel (two's complement), 8000 ticks a second at 1x, no touch note (any jog message = touched).
// The name must not contain "ReaScratch" (reascratch_lib.lua finds the engine by that name).
//
// Relative mode only (the record's speed and direction; the bits that give the absolute place are not read): the
// carrier is a quadrature tone (1 kHz at 33 1/3 rpm for Serato and rekordbox, 2 kHz Traktor, 1.3 kHz MixVibes), one
// channel 90 degrees from the other; its phase atan2(L, R) turns once a carrier cycle, forward one way, backward the
// other. The phase is followed sample by sample (the amplitude, which carries the bits, drops out of atan2), so a turn
// of the record is read to a fraction of a cycle. Written from the signal's description, not from another decoder's code.
// (⚪214) Which way is forward, from xwax's timecoder.c (its direction test copied into Python, tools/q214/xwax_dir.py):
// Serato, rekordbox and Traktor go forward while atan2(L, R) grows; MixVibes the other way (its SWITCH_PHASE alone), so
// with MixVibes chosen the direction is turned round here and Direction Normal still means forward.
//
// While "Reading" is on it sends a jog message at least every 20 ms (0 = still), so the deck stays touched: the deck
// follows the record (a record held still = the deck still, as with a hand on a jog). Off = it sends nothing: after the
// deck's Auto release the deck plays by itself again.

slider1:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Reading
slider2:0<0,2,1{Serato / rekordbox (1 kHz),Traktor (2 kHz),MixVibes (1.3 kHz)}>Timecode
slider3:0<0,1,1{33 1/3 rpm,45 rpm}>Record speed
slider4:0<0,1,1{Normal,Reversed (swap if forward plays backward)}>Direction
slider5:-50<-80,-10,1>Signal threshold (dB)
slider6:1<1,16,1>MIDI channel (the deck's)
slider7:34<0,127,1>Jog CC
slider10:0<-20,20,0.001>Speed (x, read only)
slider11:-150<-150,0,0.1>Signal level (dB, read only)
slider12:0<0,100000000,1>-Ticks sent (read)

in_pin:left
in_pin:right
out_pin:left
out_pin:right

@init
ext_noinit = 1;   // REAPER's play / seek must not reset the count (the deck would jump)
TPS = 8000;       // jog ticks a second at 1x (the preset's "Jog ticks per second")
dv_pl = 0; dv_pr = 0; dv_xl = 0; dv_xr = 0;   // DC blockers
dv_ph = 0; dv_cyc = 0; dv_sent = 0;             // last phase, cycles moved (unwrapped), ticks sent
dv_env = 0; dv_spd = 0; dv_last = 0; dv_si = 0;
dv_hp = exp(-2 * $pi * 5 / srate);             // 5 Hz: the record's rumble and the input's DC, below a slow scratch's carrier
dv_ea = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.02 * srate));          // level, 20 ms
dv_sa = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.05 * srate));          // shown speed, 50 ms

// the ticks owed: sent in 63s at most (two's complement CC: 1..63 forward, 127..65 backward)
function dv_flush(o) local(t, d) (
  t = floor(dv_cyc * TPS / dv_f0 + 0.5);
  d = t - dv_sent;
  d != 0 || o - dv_last >= 0.02 * srate ? (
    d == 0 ? midisend(o, 0xB0 | dv_ch, slider7, 0) :
    while (d != 0) (
      t = max(-63, min(63, d));
      midisend(o, 0xB0 | dv_ch, slider7, t < 0 ? 128 + t : t);
      dv_sent += t; d -= t; slider12 += abs(t);
    );
    dv_last = o;
  );
);

@slider
dv_f0 = (slider2 == 1 ? 2000 : slider2 == 2 ? 1300 : 1000) * (slider3 ? 1.35 : 1);
dv_thr = 10 ^ (slider5 / 20);

@block
dv_si = 0;
dv_ch = max(0, min(15, slider6 - 1));

@sample
// DC blocked
dv_xl = spl0 - dv_pl + dv_hp * dv_xl; dv_pl = spl0;
dv_xr = spl1 - dv_pr + dv_hp * dv_xr; dv_pr = spl1;
dv_a = sqrt(dv_xl * dv_xl + dv_xr * dv_xr);
dv_env += (dv_a - dv_env) * dv_ea;
dv_p = slider4 != (slider2 == 2) ? atan2(dv_xr, dv_xl) : atan2(dv_xl, dv_xr);   // (MixVibes: the other way, see the top)
dv_d = dv_p - dv_ph; dv_ph = dv_p;
dv_d > $pi ? dv_d -= 2 * $pi : dv_d < -$pi ? dv_d += 2 * $pi;
// below the threshold the phase is noise: the record stands (or the needle is up)
dv_m = slider1 && dv_a > dv_thr && dv_env > dv_thr ? dv_d / (2 * $pi) : 0;
dv_cyc += dv_m;
dv_spd += (dv_m * srate / dv_f0 - dv_spd) * dv_sa;
slider1 && ((dv_si & 15) == 15 || dv_si == samplesblock - 1) ? dv_flush(dv_si);
dv_si += 1;
dv_si == samplesblock ? (
  dv_last -= samplesblock;   // dv_last counts from the next block's start
  slider10 = dv_spd;
  slider11 = dv_env > 0 ? max(-150, 20 * log10(dv_env)) : -150;
);
spl0 = spl1 = 0;   // the tone is not heard
